jobs.description:
Setting up machines, monitoring the packaging process and supervising colleagues on the line? As a Packaging Operator at Bobeldijk in Deventer, you will be responsible for your own packaging line. And you’ll earn from €17.17 gross per hour, excluding shift allowance.

You make sure the line keeps running, set up the machines correctly and step in when a malfunction occurs. At the same time, you monitor product quality and work together with 2 to 3 colleagues to make sure production stays on schedule.

Could this be your next challenge?

Wat wordt er van je verwacht
As a Operator Packaging, you make sure the packaging line runs smoothly. You know the machines, understand what needs to be produced and keep an overview of the entire process.

Your tasks include:
- Setting up and operating packaging machines;
- Adjusting and converting machines for product changes;
- Monitoring the packaging process;
- Checking the quality of the finished products;
- Identifying and resolving minor technical issues;
- Supervising and supporting 2 to 3 colleagues on your line;
- Keeping your workplace clean, safe and organised.

Your job involves more than just operating machines. You also divide tasks, work closely with your colleagues and make sure production stays on schedule.

You will work full-time in a 2-shift system, alternating between morning shifts and afternoon/evening shifts.

Wat zoeken wij
We are looking for someone who is comfortable taking responsibility and interested in understanding how machines and production processes work.

In addition:
- You have MBO level 2 or 3, or an equivalent level of education;
- You have an interest in technology and production;
- You are available full-time and able to work in a 2-shift system;
- You work accurately and know how to keep an overview;
- You work well in a team and are comfortable supervising colleagues on the line;
- You speak Dutch and/or English.

