Your responsibilities will include:

- Loading and unloading goods;
- Moving and stacking pallets;
- Processing and handling products within the warehouse;
- Lifting and moving boxes weighing up to 23 kg;
- Maintaining a clean, safe, and organized workspace.

You will also perform various Value Added Services (VAS), such as:

- Applying stickers and labels to products;
- Repacking and packaging items;
- Preparing products for shipment;
- Inflating and preparing sports and recreational products for distribution.

You will primarily work in a day shift from 07:00 AM – 04:00 PM. During peak periods in July till October, a two-shift schedule will apply:

- 06:00 AM – 03:00 PM
- 03:00 PM – 12:00 AM
- A 12.5% shift allowance applies during these periods.

You are someone who enjoys physical work and likes to stay active throughout the day.

Additionally, you:

- Are physically fit and enjoy hands-on work;
- Are available to work fulltime and can commit to a fixed work schedule;
- Are flexible and willing to work shifts during peak in July till October;
- Have an EPT certificate or are willing to obtain one;
- Live in Helmond or nearby;
- Have a good command of Dutch and/or English;
- Are motivated and reliable.

As a Production Employee at Bavaria in Lieshout, you will play an important role in brewing and packaging one of the Netherlands' most iconic beers. In our state-of-the-art bottling facility, you help fill approximately 100,000 cans and bottles every hour.

Working at Bavaria means being involved in the entire production process. Together with your colleagues, you ensure that production runs as smoothly and efficiently as possible. Your shift starts and ends with a handover, where you discuss production results, breakdowns, and other important details with operators from the other teams.

At Bavaria, you will enjoy a varied role with responsibilities including:

- Setting up and adjusting machines;
- Troubleshooting common technical issues;
- Performing maintenance on the production line;
- Sorting returnable bottles;
- Supplying packaging machines with caps and rolls;
- Monitoring and checking beer quality.

Working Hours & Availability

Until January, you will work in a fixed 3-shift rotation with a repeating three-week cycle:

- Week 1: 4 to 5 night shifts from 10:00 PM to 06:00 AM
- Week 2: 3 afternoon shifts from 02:00 PM to 10:00 PM and 2 morning shifts from 06:00 AM to 02:00 PM
- Week 3: 3 morning shifts from 06:00 AM to 02:00 PM and 2 afternoon shifts from 02:00 PM to 10:00 PM

From January onwards, you will transition to a fixed 5-shift rotation schedule:

- 2 early shifts from 06:00 AM to 02:00 PM
- 2 late shifts from 02:00 PM to 10:00 PM
- 2 night shifts from 10:00 PM to 06:00 AM
- 4 days off

Are you ready to become part of this dynamic family-owned company? Apply now and you could soon be working in the bottling facility of Royal Swinkels!

- You are available to work in a 5-shift rotation schedule and till januari in a 3-shift schedule; 
- You have a good command of either the Dutch or English language;
- You are eager to learn and develop new skills.

Summary

Are you detail-oriented, technically minded and do you enjoy working with your hands? Would you like to join one of Europe’s leading manufacturers of custom-made sandwich panels? Then this position with our client in Waalwijk could be the perfect opportunity for you.

Job Description

As a Production Worker, you will contribute to the manufacturing of high-quality, tailor-made sandwich panels. These panels are used in various industries, including bodywork construction and defense. Depending on your experience, interests and the needs of the department, you will be assigned to different tasks within the production process.

You will work from Monday to Friday, from 07:00 to 16:00, as part of a close-knit and supportive team. Using technical drawings and parts lists, you will transform individual raw materials into a finished product of excellent quality. Thanks to the variety of panels and tasks, no two working days are the same.

Accuracy, quality and teamwork are key within this role. The impact of your work is directly visible in the final product.

Responsibilities

Depending on the department, your tasks may include:

- Emptying, cleaning and preparing press tables;
- Collecting and preparing various raw materials;
- Producing and bonding sandwich panels;
- Cutting, deburring and sealing aluminum panels;
- Sawing, calibrating and adjusting materials such as foam, wood and composite to the correct thickness;
- Numbering, sorting and preparing parts for shipment;
- Operating machinery and, if qualified, an overhead crane;
- Maintaining a clean and safe working environment.

What We Ask

- You work accurately and have technical insight;
- You can read technical drawings and parts lists, or are willing to learn;
- You are a true team player;
- You have a good command of Dutch and/or English.
